  "about": "In my current role as a Senior Developer for Infrastructure as Code, I led the design and launch of automations that accelerated application delivery to a hybrid data center. I also developed a reusable infrastructure template catalog, significantly reducing the time required to host applications reliably.\n\nI am also passionate about web development. I introduced new patterns and approaches that improved our team’s efficiency and code quality. My innovative use of technology resulted in engaging websites supporting teams with complex requirements.\n\nAs a software professional with a non-traditional, hands-on education, I've witnessed ineffective development practices. Early in my career, I often heard: \"Make a website for our client, we need it by the end of the month.\" These experiences sparked my interest in efficient web design and development.\n\nDelivering efficiently means little without a quality end product. No matter the methodology, the true measure of success is the audience's response. \n\nI began as a machine operator, then advanced to a prepress operator, and eventually became a digital print production engineer. This progression exposed me to a variety of printing projects, from simple mail merges to complex PDF generation. My technical foundation in print production now complements my web development skills.\n\nI began by using solutions for variable print production, such as Xerox xData, em Software's XData, and Printables' Fusion Pro. Over time, I progressed to building custom solutions with APIs.\n\nSpecialties:\n\nInfrastructure as Code:\n\n* Languages: Terraform, Bicep, Yaml, Docker\n* Platforms/Tools: Azure Devops, ArgoCD, Azure, KeyFactor, Cloudflare, Delinea Secret Server, Infoblox\n\nWeb Development:\n\n* Languages: HTML, XHTML, XML, JavaScript, CSS, LESS\n* Tools: VSCode, Visual Studio, Node.js/Grunt\n\nBack-End:\n\n* Platforms: IIS, MS SQL Server, ASP.NET MVC. Kubernetes, Azure\n* Languages: C#, WSH, T-SQL, Bash, Powershell, Helm, Yaml\n* Tools: VSCode, Visual Studio\n\nActive Learning:\n\n* AngularJS, MongoDB, Express, Node (The Mean Stack)\n* UX, Test Driven Development (TDD), Agile",
